  THE DECLARATION -- WRITTEN AND COMMITTED BEFORE ANY FIT RAN (several
  declarations of a batch share one commit).

  IDENTITY.  nHexane (CAS 110-54-3, InChIKey VLKZOEOYAKHREP-UHFFFAOYSA-N)
  + 2Butanol (CAS 78-92-2, InChIKey BTANRVKWQNVYAZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N), joined
  to the archive through identity.json -- never by name.  CLASS (C284): both
  records are volatile molecular liquids (no role nonvolatile/solute, no
  dissociatesTo, no charge, no solid, a vapour-pressure model), and every
  measured temperature lies below both critical temperatures.

  NO MEASURED SERIES IN THIS TREE.  constant/archiveDatasets names each
  dataset (DOI, NIST URL, article sha256, extraction selector, extract
  sha256); `bin/choupo-curate fetch` writes the points into
  constant/archiveExtracts/, which is gitignored.

  STUDIES: every isothermal bubble-pressure block of the pair at or below
  110 kPa that states an uncertainty on every point.  FITTED, ALL OF THEM
  (2 block(s), 2 laboratory(ies), 2 temperature(s)):
      10.1021/acs.jced.9b00102       block 15   58 pts  329.15 K  14.56-68.68 kPa  U 0.29-0.63 kPa
      10.1016/j.fluid.2011.08.009    block 6    26 pts  329.22 K  15.31-68.83 kPa  U 0.2-1.15 kPa
        (reports x of the other member: written as x[nHexane] = 1 - x by --x-of)
  SET ASIDE BY THE EXTRACTION RULES, BY NAME:
      - doi 10.1021/acs.jced.7b00892 block 15: extract-px refused it: THE
      TEMPERATURE VARIES ACROSS THE POINTS (2 values, 329.2 .. 329.21 K);
      this reader takes one isotherm per block (a ruling is needed to
      read a multi-isotherm block).
      - doi 10.1021/acs.jced.9b00102 block 13: extract-px refused it: THE
      TEMPERATURE VARIES ACROSS THE POINTS (3 values, 303.15 .. 343.15
      K); this reader takes one isotherm per block (a ruling is needed to
      read a multi-isotherm block).
      - doi 10.1021/je900530f block 4: extract-px refused it: THE
      TEMPERATURE VARIES ACROSS THE POINTS (3 values, 313.15 .. 333.15
      K); this reader takes one isotherm per block (a ruling is needed to
      read a multi-isotherm block).

  THE RULE (DEV.md 4c C291, bubble-pressure pairs).  Every block above is
  fitted together; none is held out.  NRTL, a_ij = a_ji = 0, alpha = 0.30
  fixed: two parameters (b_ij, b_ji), so tau = b/T carries the temperature
  dependence.  The residual is the bubble PRESSURE at each point's stated
  temperature, RELATIVE, (P_model - P)/P; objective twoStage (least squares,
  then minimax; P_bubble relative).  OUTLIERS: after a least-squares stage over
  every point, a point with |P_model - P|/P > 20 % is discarded BY NAME
  (`discard` on its evidence entry, listed below) and the fit repeated
  without it; a STUDY with more than half of its points beyond 20 % is
  discarded whole, by name (it contradicts the model and the other
  laboratories as a whole, e.g. a composition labelled as the other member's).
  THE GRADED ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C285, in per cent of P): max |P_model - P|/P over the KEPT points is GRADED -- clean up to 5 %, warning up to 10 %, severe up to 20 %, refused above; a point with no bubble pressure refuses.  Every grade but refused is accepted and promoted (autoPromoted, humanReviewed false) with `fitGrade` and its max relative error in the record's provenance; the engine voices a warning or a severe grade on every run that reads the pair.  A pair that splits ONE liquid inside its validity span is not promoted, whatever its grade (arm f).
  Two starts: (0, 0) and (800, -400).  The per-point uncertainty U (kPa) is
  kept in each dataset and is information: this residual is already relative.

